<?php
namespace App\Services\Marketing;

/** Narrative boundaries, independent of tone, presentation, models and spending. */
class MarketingVideoFormPolicy
{
 public const VERSION='video-form-boundaries-v1';
 public function catalog():array {return [
  'product_showcase'=>['label'=>'商品展示','direction'=>'Product-led: reveal the whole product, then meaningful visible details, then context or closure. Strong recognition and appearance; limited narrative depth. Avoid empty rotating shots and generic adjective lists.'],
  'scenario_story'=>['label'=>'场景故事','direction'=>'Story-led: a recognizable situation, a small need or tension, an action, and a change or resolution. Product enters naturally. Strong identification; do not let the story obscure the product. Not an explanation chopped into locations. No invented product benefits or fake testimonials; a person need not appear on screen.'],
  'tutorial'=>['label'=>'教学说明','direction'=>'Learning-led: a clear achievable learning goal, preparation, executable ordered steps, key caution and completion. Strong practical clarity; avoid overload, missing steps and unsupported instructions.'],
  'feature_demo'=>['label'=>'功能演示','direction'=>'Demonstration-led: a specific task, observable operation, actual function response and visible result. Strong concrete understanding; avoid invented functionality and decorative shots replacing proof of the operation.'],
  'service_intro'=>['label'=>'服务介绍','direction'=>'Service-led: who needs it, scope, process, deliverables and how to begin. Strong service clarity and trust; avoid corporate slogans, invented case studies, guarantees and out-of-scope promises.'],
  'presenter'=>['label'=>'人物口播','direction'=>'Speaker-led: a hook, useful explanation or viewpoint, and a natural next step. Direct communication; avoid monotonous catalog reading. May borrow a small story or demonstration, but retain the speaker as the primary experience and respect selected identity.'],
 ];}
 public function type(array $facts):string {return $facts['concept']['video_type']??$facts['preferences']['video_type']??'auto';}
 public function instruction(string $type):string {
  $all=$this->catalog();$selected=isset($all[$type])?[$type=>$all[$type]]:$all;
  return 'VIDEO FORM POLICY '.self::VERSION.'. Form is the primary content organization, not marketing goal, tone or a requirement to show a person. Supporting techniques may combine; retain the selected primary form. Scale structure to duration, not a rigid template. '.json_encode($selected,JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE|JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR).' Creative quality is advisory; do not invent facts, media, permissions or prices. '.$this->coordinationInstruction();
 }
 public function coordinationInstruction():string {return 'PACING COORDINATION v1. Design duration, useful spoken copy, subtitle reading load and visible story beats together from the concept stage through the director draft. A longer video needs additional meaningful story development, explanation or demonstrable actions, not the same short slogans stretched across more seconds. In concept story/reason describe how the confirmed length is supported; in director rhythm use realistic estimated speaking windows and specify what changes on screen during each non-speaking interval. For scenario_story develop situation, need, choice and resolution in conversational language; do not substitute official product slogans for story. Estimate copy length before assigning windows; do not label a two-second sentence as eight seconds of speech. Compare both per-scene and whole-film coverage. Sparse narration is a review signal, not a mandatory speech quota: deliberate visual stories, demonstrations and silent films remain valid when supported by specific observable beats. Do not invent such actions if saved visuals are locked. If time is unsupported, add useful copy only within the requested rewrite scope and known facts, or recommend a shorter duration; preserve locked/authored text, timing and visual assets and report the mismatch. No automatic rewrite, retry, new generation or fee. Subtitles may follow exact narration or concise complementary on-screen information; budget readable display time, avoid overload, production instructions and needless full-shot text holds. No narration does not mean no subtitles; subtitles are not a replacement for weak story. Every long silence needs a specific observable action, viewer reading task, emotional change or transition plus its duration; generic atmosphere/hold/pause labels are insufficient evidence. Estimates are not measured TTS or proof of good pacing; later use actual audio without stretching speech or changing composition rules.';}
 public function rhythmInstruction():string {return ' Plan speech and intentional silence together. Estimate mixed CJK/punctuation characters at 4 per second plus Latin words at 2.5 per second; this is not measured audio. Never fill time with empty slogans or force nonstop speech. New scene rhythm: speech_start/speech_end in LOCAL seconds, silent_beats [{start,end,purpose}], reason. Speech window and purposeful silent beats must cover scene time exactly without overlaps/gaps; no speech uses a zero-length speech window. Silence must serve an observable action, observation/environment sound, transition, emphasis or reading time. Explain why it serves this form. Do not rewrite locked/authored copy or seconds; flag a mismatch rather than fake alignment. Real generated audio needs later timing verification.';}
}
